>When you are invisible, things like goblins still throw their
>knives at you when you are in line, but they still move around
>randomly. If the goblins can not see me, why do they still
>throw their knives at me? If they can hear me, how come they
>don't move in my general direction?

Actually they don't.  Not do they use breath weapons that way.  They throw
or breathe at their best guess as to where your position is--it's quite
possible to suddenly see a weapon appear at your side, thrown by a monster that
guessed wrong.

However, if you stay in one position (not moving), monsters will in a few
moves figure out where you are.
